===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{etyl|ur|en}} {{term|مغل|tr=muġal|lang=ur}}, variant of {{term|مغل|tr=muġul|lang=ur}}, from {{etyl|fa|en}} {{term|مغول|tr=muġul|lang=fa}}, from {{etyl|mn|en}} {{term||tr=mongɣol|lang=mn}}. In early use via various European languages.{{attention|ur}} {{attention|mn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A head of the Mongolian [[dynasty]] founded by Zahīr-ud-Dīn Muhammed Bābur (1483-1530) which controlled large parts of southern Asia from the 16th to the 19th centuries.
# {{context|now|_|historical}} A [[Mongol]] or [[Mongolian]], especially a member or follower of the Moghul dynasty.
# An [[important]] or [[successful]] person; a [[magnate]]. (Now usually as {{term|mogul}})

